# What `railway up` must not upload.
#
# The CLI sends the working directory, not the git tree, so anything sitting on
# disk goes with it unless excluded. Without this the upload is 221 MB of local
# build artefacts to deploy roughly 2 MB of source -- and a virtualenv built on
# macOS is actively harmful in a Linux container if it were ever unpacked there.
#
# Railway applies the service's root directory (backend) to what arrives, so
# run `railway up` from the repository root, not from backend/.

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

dist/
**/dist/
.vite/
**/.vite/

.git/
.claude/
.vercel/
**/.vercel/

# Secrets live in Railway's own variables, never in an upload.
.env
**/.env
.env.local
**/.env.local
